IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cda-nouns`

-- Criminal Damage Act 1971, section 10: INTERPRETATION.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Written from the text alone.
--
-- Section 10 comes last in the Act but is the dictionary for sections 1 to 3,
-- so its module comes before theirs in this encoding. What it settles:
--   * s 10(1): what is "property";
--   * s 10(2) to (4): when property is treated as "belonging to" a person;
--   * s 10(5): when changing the contents of a computer is "damaging" it.
-- Each rule takes the facts about one thing (Thing, Connection, Damage in
-- cda-nouns.l4) and answers the Act's own question from them.

§ `Section 10 -- Interpretation`

§§ `10(1) -- property`

-- src:51 | 10 Interpretation.
-- src:52 | (1) In this Act “property” means property of a tangible nature, whether real or personal, including money and—
-- src:53 | (a) including wild creatures which have been tamed or are ordinarily kept in captivity, and any other wild creatures or their carcasses if, but only if, they have been reduced into possession which has not been lost or abandoned or are in the course of being reduced into possession; but
-- src:54 | (b) not including mushrooms growing wild on any land or flowers, fruit or foliage of a plant growing wild on any land.
-- src:55 | For the purposes of this subsection “mushroom” includes any fungus and “plant” includes any shrub or tree.
@ref s 10(1) (src:51-55)
GIVEN thing IS A Thing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a thing is property within section 10(1)` thing MEANS
        (   (    thing's `of a tangible nature`
             AND (NOT (thing's `any other wild creature, or the carcass of a wild creature`)))
         OR thing's `money`
         OR `10(1)(a): a wild creature tamed or ordinarily kept in captivity` thing
         OR `10(1)(a): another wild creature or a carcass, reduced or being reduced into possession` thing)
    AND (NOT (`10(1)(b): a mushroom, or flowers, fruit or foliage of a plant, growing wild` thing))

-- The first limb of (a): tamed or ordinarily kept in captivity. Such a creature is property.
@ref s 10(1)(a) (src:53)
GIVEN thing IS A Thing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`10(1)(a): a wild creature tamed or ordinarily kept in captivity` thing MEANS
    thing's `a wild creature tamed or ordinarily kept in captivity`

-- The second limb of (a): "if, but only if". Any other wild creature, or a carcass,
-- is property only while reduced into possession (not lost or abandoned) or being reduced.
@ref s 10(1)(a) (src:53)
GIVEN thing IS A Thing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`10(1)(a): another wild creature or a carcass, reduced or being reduced into possession` thing MEANS
        thing's `any other wild creature, or the carcass of a wild creature`
    AND (   thing's `reduced into possession which has not been lost or abandoned`
         OR thing's `in the course of being reduced into possession`)

-- (b): never property. "Mushroom" includes any fungus and "plant" includes any shrub
-- or tree (the last sentence of s 10(1)); the field names in cda-nouns.l4 already say so.
@ref s 10(1)(b) (src:54-55)
GIVEN thing IS A Thing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`10(1)(b): a mushroom, or flowers, fruit or foliage of a plant, growing wild` thing MEANS
        thing's `a mushroom, including any fungus, growing wild on any land`
    OR  thing's `flowers, fruit or foliage of a plant, including a shrub or tree, growing wild on any land`

§§ `10(2) to (4) -- belonging to a person`

-- src:56 | (2) Property shall be treated for the purposes of this Act as belonging to any person—
-- src:57 | (a) having the custody or control of it;
-- src:58 | (b) having in it any proprietary right or interest (not being an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest); or
-- src:59 | (c) having a charge on it.
-- src:60 | (3) Where property is subject to a trust, the persons to whom it belongs shall be so treated as including any person having a right to enforce the trust.
-- src:61 | (4) Property of a corporation sole shall be so treated as belonging to the corporation notwithstanding a vacancy in the corporation.
@ref s 10(2) to (4) (src:56-61)
GIVEN connection IS A Connection
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`property belongs to a person with this connection under section 10(2) to (4)` connection MEANS
        connection's `custody or control of it`
    OR  (connection's `interest in it` EQUALS `a proprietary right or interest`)
    OR  connection's `a charge on it`
    OR  connection's `a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject`
    OR  connection's `the corporation sole whose property it is, whether or not there is a vacancy in the corporation`

-- "Another" is a person other than the accused. Property can belong to several
-- persons at once (s 10(2): "any person"), so property that belongs to the accused
-- and to someone else also "belongs to another". See NOTES.md, fork F4.
@ref s 10(2) to (4), applied to property within s 10(1) (src:56-61)
GIVEN property IS A `Property facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`property belonging to another` property MEANS
        `a thing is property within section 10(1)` (property's `the thing`)
    AND any `property belongs to a person with this connection under section 10(2) to (4)` (property's `other persons' connections with it`)

@ref s 10(2) to (4), applied to property within s 10(1) (src:56-61)
GIVEN property IS A `Property facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`property belonging to the accused` property MEANS
        `a thing is property within section 10(1)` (property's `the thing`)
    AND `property belongs to a person with this connection under section 10(2) to (4)` (property's `the accused's connection with it`)

§§ `10(5) -- computers`

-- src:62 | (5) For the purposes of this Act a modification of the contents of a computer shall not be regarded as damaging any computer or computer storage medium unless its effect on that computer or computer storage medium impairs its physical condition.
@ref s 10(5) (src:62)
GIVEN damage IS A Damage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`destruction or damage within the Act` damage MEANS
        damage's `destruction or damage`
    AND (   (NOT (damage's `by a modification of the contents of a computer or computer storage medium alone`))
         OR damage's `with an effect that impairs the physical condition of the computer or computer storage medium`)
